# combase: Fix IContextCallback::ContextCallback() into another apartment.
# https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/merge_requests/12732 state=closed
# C++/WinRT's apartment_context and resume_foreground() use ContextCallback() to get back to an apartment. On Wine this fails with RPC_E_DISCONNECTED when the target apartment hasn't marshalled anything yet, because its IRundown is never exported, so the callback never runs. Minecraft Bedrock hits this when importing a world.

The fix exports IRundown from CoGetContextToken(), on the apartment's own thread. I first tried starting remoting from the caller instead, but that deadlocks when the target is a second STA.

With calls getting through, the new tests turned up a second bug: the callback sometimes saw a freshly generated logical thread id instead of the caller's, depending on which RPC thread handled the call. That's fixed in rpc_execute_call(), which also lets an existing todo_wine in test_CoGetObjectContext() go.

I tested on macOS with both 64-bit and 32-bit (wow64) builds. The ole32, combase and msvcp140 tests show no new failures at any commit, and compobj passed 20 runs in a row on each. Reverting any part of either fix makes the new tests fail. dragdrop is flaky on master and is no worse with this.

### Not tested

- Windows, Linux.
